I've written about this in a few posts lately, but to restate:
getting teleport control from tengu corpses is far from guaranteed.
Sometimes you get TC from the first corpse, sometimes you don't get it
even after several magic markers.  If you want TC and have a free ring
finger and a spare wish, just wish for the ring.  Once you have the
intrinsic from chance encounters or are on the planes you can ditch
the ring.  The decision, IMO, comes down to evaluating what are your
most available resources.  Then use wishes or markers or ring-fingers
as appropriate.  For me, I rarely need a late game ring of slow
digestion and just wear free action with conflict and levitation at
the ready.  That leaves a ring-finger free for TC.

Regarding potion dipping.  I prefer dipping with boots of water
walking rather than diving because I'm paranoid and with maxed luck it
feels like it takes too long to dilute my potions.  It's fewer
keystrokes to use water walking boots.  But it's up to the individual
and I'm not saying that I would wish for WW, but I do prize them when
I find them.

Judging by the prose and content of your (the OP, that is) post, I'd
recommend slowing down a bit.  Unless you are having food supply
issues there shouldn't be any harm in setting up neat stashes on
various levels and when burdened make a new stash or head back to
base.

You're really far in the game.  Stay focused and you're likely to
ascend.  Good luck!
